0808031763881445], ["/service", -5.5290327072143555]]}], "text": "Here's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part session (Context A: Claude Opus 5.5, 09-26 to 09-28; Context B: Claude Sonnet 5.5, resumed 10-01) rebuilt the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) across commits b10146 \u2192 b12321 on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D, 64GB DDR5, Intel Arc A770 16GB, Arch Linux).\n\n- **Driver switch:** The A770 moved from the i915 driver (Context A) to the **xe** driver (Context B) between sessions, driven by other sessions; the AMD iGPU continues to drive the monitors.\n\n- **Major technical work:** Included a PKGBUILD rework, debugging a `LLAMA_SUBPROCESS` ABI trap (commit d37dd50bb), SYCL graphs, a oneDNN A/B test, a oneAPI 2026.0 \u2192 2026.1 swap (DLE swap), reviewing PR #63, and patching a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash (commit 4e7400c3a).\n\n- **Performance investigation:** A key focus was a \"12-vs-18 t/s decode investigation,\" plus 256-GRF kernel builds, perplexity A/B testing, and GRF llama-bench attempts.\n\n- **Documentation rigor:** The record is heavily cross-referenced with evidence files (SHA-256 verified), live re-checks of repo/package/system"}